## 20. MVP Definition of Done

The MVP is "done" when a new player can:

1. Wake up in the apartment, learn the basic loop in their first in-game day
2. Encounter Erik on the way out and learn about Hank
3. Accept Hank's fronted ounce and feel the week-1 debt timer
4. Find a dealing spot, read passersby, complete street deals
5. Get busted on a street deal at least once and feel the cumulative-heat consequence
6. Buy a scale from Felix and feel the eyeball-tax-removed margin improvement
7. Pay Hank back by Sunday end-of-day and trigger the pivot event
8. Buy a pager from Felix (week 2)
9. Receive a page, return the call, complete a deal, get paid at retail
10. Develop a recurring buyer relationship over multiple successful pager deals
11. Grow weed from seed to harvest over an in-game week
12. Loot at least one car successfully
13. Reach Tier 1 in each XP track (DealerExperience, CriminalExperience)
14. Develop one player skill to a meaningful threshold and feel the capability change
15. Build relationship with at least one of the named NPCs to a meaningful threshold
16. Encounter Tyrone at the school corner spot and make the deal-or-don't choice; see Rosa's dialogue respond
17. Survive (or fail to survive) a full in-game month including rent obligations
18. Save and reload without state loss

If all eighteen are achievable in a vertical slice, MVP is done and "is this loop fun?" can be answered with real playtest data.

