## 22. Gotchas & Conventions

[Retained from v0.8 — Godot quirks, save/load patterns, outdoor chunking, tween coordination, asset pipeline conventions, input handling, animation naming, known minor bugs.]

Additions in v0.9:
- **Cross-autoload signal wiring** needs `call_deferred` in the listener's `_ready` if the emitter loads later. See §17. Symptom: "Identifier not declared" or null reference on the emitter during the listener's `_ready`.
additions in V1.0:
- **Typed arrays of Resource subclasses across script boundaries.** `Array[ItemDef]` won't accept `PlaceableItemDef` instances reliably in some contexts (typically vendor `initial_stock` arrays in the inspector). Same problem applies to `Array[CustomerArchetype]` parameters on autoload functions. Workaround: declare the parameter and storage var as plain `Array` (untyped) or `Array[Resource]` for inspector typing. Internal usage can still cast back to the subclass.

additions in V1.1:
- **Typed array param mismatch on `set_patrol`.** Passing an untyped `Array` to a function declared `Array[Vector2]` errors ("array of argument does not have the same element type"). Declare the local as `Array[Vector2]` before appending.
- **Group lookup in `_ready` vs. node order.** A scene-root controller that `add_to_group()`s in its own `_ready` is registered *after* its children's `_ready` (children run first). Children that need the controller must resolve it lazily (on interact) or `call_deferred`, not cache it in their `_ready` — the cached lookup is null. (Hit by drink stations finding the bar controller.)
- **Held-state interaction eligibility needs a manual re-arbitration poke.** `can_interact` filters work, but picking up/dropping a non-physical "held" item doesn't fire `state_changed` or a zone enter/exit, so the InteractionManager won't recompute. Call `InteractionManager.notify_player_state_changed()` after the state change. (Bar carry-one-drink.)
- **Two clocks: game-time vs. real-delta.** Minigame *session length* should ride game-time (`total_minutes`, or `push_speed` to accelerate the world), but moment-to-moment *gameplay timers* (progress bars, patience) should run on raw `delta`. Keeping them separate is what lets a shift's world-time accelerate while drinks/patience stay at human pace.
- **Id tokens vs. display text.** Keep internal ids clean tokens (`beer`) and map display names separately (`"Beer"`). Putting prompt/display text into an id field silently breaks equality matching elsewhere (e.g. `held_drink() == order` never matches). Hit when a station's `drink_type` inspector field was filled with the prompt string.
- **`push_speed`/`pop_speed` must be paired across scene teardown.** Pop in `_exit_tree` (guarded by a `_pushed` bool) so an early scene exit can't leave the world running fast. Same discipline as the street minigame.
- **`set_global_flag` only emits on actual change.** `RelationshipSystem.global_flag_changed` fires only when the value differs from before. A listener that needs to catch an already-set flag (e.g. set before the listener's `_ready` connected, or re-set to the same value) must also check the flag directly in its own `_ready`. (EmploymentSystem catches an already-true `has_job` this way.)
- **Tilesets moved between folders break `ext_resource` paths / UIDs.** Reverting the file moves doesn't always restore the import cache. Symptom: scenes parse-error on a missing `.tres` at runtime though it's fine in-editor. Fix: close Godot, delete the `.godot/` folder (all derived data), reopen to force a clean reimport + UID rebuild.
- **Inventory `slots` array sized from inspector, not from `max_slots` assignment.** When a Node assigns `inventory.max_slots = N` in its own `_ready`, the Inventory child's `_ready` has already run with whatever the *scene file* set max_slots to. The internal `slots` array doesn't resize on the int reassignment. Symptom: vendor with `stock_size = 24` only stocks the first 3 items. Fix: also call `stock.slots.clear()` and `stock.slots.resize(stock_size)` after the assignment, or override `max_slots` to resize on set.
- **`TimeSkipSystem.skip_to` is async** — it awaits internal fade tweens and fires `time_skipped` while the screen is black. Listeners hook `time_skipped` to do their work during the dark window (position changes, stat restores). Callers that want to do post-skip work should either await skip_to (if they're also async) or hook the signal.
- **Cop pursuit can fire on cops the caller thinks it's "detached" from.** `PoliceSystem.unregister_cop` only removes from PoliceSystem's dicts. The cop's `WitnessComponent` is still registered with `WitnessRegistry`, and `CrimeSystem.dispatch_pursuit` looks up cops via the witness pipeline, not PoliceSystem. To fully detach: also `WitnessRegistry.unregister(wc)` or destroy the WitnessComponent. Or — as we did in the street deal minigame — leave it active because the minigame *wants* witness-triggered busts, and accept that pursuit may briefly fire on the puppet cops (harmless since the scene tears down immediately on bust).
- **Stamina sprint multiplier.** When wiring new multipliers onto velocity, use the locally-built `move_multiplier` (which already includes skill + sprint). Re-fetching `PlayerSkills.speed_multiplier()` in the final velocity assignment silently drops the sprint factor. Pattern: build `move_multiplier` up incrementally, use it once.

